# Linear Sensors — a Skia "app icon" (rounded square + React logo) tilted in
# 3D by the device's rotation (roll) and gravity (z) sensors through
# useAnimatedSensor at 20 ms, with a drop shadow that moves with the tilt.
# What this test covers: the sensor-driven worklets running for a while (the
# simulator reports a resting device), device orientation changes through all
# four orientations and back (app is portrait-locked; sensors keep streaming
# and the icon must keep rendering), and taps/drags on the canvas (no
# handlers; must be ignored). Ends back in portrait.
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/linear-sensors"
wait 2000
wait "label=\"Close\"" 30000
wait 3000
orientation landscape-left
wait 1500
orientation portrait-upside-down
wait 1500
orientation landscape-right
wait 1500
orientation portrait
wait 2000
press 201 450
wait 300
gesture pan 120 450 160 0 500
wait 500
gesture pan 201 600 0 -200 500
wait 3000
wait "label=\"Close\"" 15000
press "role=\"button\" label=\"Close\""
wait 1500
